          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: a reported event was created 75 minutes after Pending Close\n\n**This is a qualified finding:** I directly verified the work order, Pending Close timestamp, and Oracle policy. The event details below come from an accessible shared peer audit; I could not independently inspect this review’s restricted cost-event source.\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** — Cooler Plate Pack, Modine Racine |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004**, `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Event amount | **USD $284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 1 hour 15 minutes, or 4,500 seconds |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nThe timestamps are reproduced exactly as supplied; no time-zone offset was provided.\n\n### Is `POSTED` consistent with Oracle’s policy?\n\n**No, on the reported event facts.** Oracle’s *Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B*, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting” (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened.\n\nOracle allows continued processing for revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. The reported component-issue `INPUT` event is not one of those exceptions. Its `POSTED` status therefore conflicts with the documented Pending Close treatment.\n\n### Review status\n\nNo database or business-source records were changed. The report was submitted, but validation remains **`needs_evidence`** because the event details were not independently source-verified in this review.\n\nThe audit result and detailed provenance are saved at:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_5990e0cb8ff4/audit-report.json`",
